# Force LF in the working tree for every text file, on every platform.
# This app is deployed to Linux, and install.sh / app.py / the systemd
# unit must not arrive with CRLF: a shell script with CRLF fails with
# "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M". That happens if someone clones on
# Windows (where Git would otherwise check out CRLF) and copies the
# files across to their server, which is a normal way to install this.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.db binary
*.gz binary
